    "ticket_key": "GB-185",
    "slug": "concurrent-storypole-defers-allocate-the-same-ticket-key-and-poison-the-index-9b28f6",
    "title": "Concurrent storypole defers allocate the same ticket key and poison the index",
    "description": "Two defer invocations started in the same second both read max_ticket_number from the SQLite index and both allocated GB-183, so the ledger gained two events with one key and every later command failed to rebuild the index with 'UNIQUE constraint failed: tasks.ticket_key_lower'. Distinct from GB-147 (spliced ledger writes): here both events are well-formed and the ledger parses cleanly - only the key allocation races. Observed while closing GB-182; repaired by re-keying the second event to GB-184 by hand.",
    "kind": "bug",
